      "ground_truth": "Returns the maximum of prices[j] - prices[i] over j > i, or 0 when no profitable pair exists; buying and selling on the same day is not allowed.",
      "golden_response": "Reference approach (passes all 8 cases):\n\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def maxProfit(self, prices: list[int]) -> int:\n        best = 0\n        lo = prices[0]\n        for p in prices[1:]:\n            best = max(best, p - lo)\n            lo = min(lo, p)\n        return best\n```",
